        <mxCell id="legend" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;fontColor=#1D2D3E;fontFamily=Arial;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=14;" value="LEGEND   Gray: request / response   |   Green: authentication   |   Indigo: authorization" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="30" width="1770" x="40" y="1030" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="notes" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;fontColor=#1D2D3E;fontFamily=Arial;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=14;" value="IMPLEMENTATION CONDITIONS&#xa;¹ Proposed identity model: PrincipalPropagation. Configure identity mapping, certificate trust, SCC virtual host/resource mapping and S/4HANA authorizations.&#xa;² Scope: MM purchase contracts maintained in ME32K. Verify API coverage for nested service lines, conditions and prices in release 2022 FPS 02. Use a reviewed ABAP adapter if required; no direct table writes.&#xa;   Enable CSRF handling for writes; enforce SAP locking and per-contract transactions. Handle partial failures and reconcile ambiguous outcomes before retrying.&#xa;³ HANA Cloud is the selected persistence option for this proposal, not a connectivity requirement. Implement retention and access controls for uploaded data and results.&#xa;   Baseline: user-driven, bounded requests. High-volume unattended processing requires a durable worker and a separately designed background identity model.&#xa;   Deployment: configure service bindings, xs-app.json routes, HTML5 app-host/app-runtime, HDI container, roles, application logs and monitoring.&#xa;Architecture review only: no deployment or end-to-end SAP test performed. Official SAP icon library: SAP/btp-solution-diagrams." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="165" width="1770" x="40" y="1090" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
